      "replacements": [
        [
          "Row contribution/reconstruction work is O(kd), selected contribution alone O(d); requested all-row reconstruction is O(nkd), and its n×d output is itself a storage cost.",
          "For already validated factors, reconstructing one row takes O(kd), while multiplying one selected amount by its length-d pattern takes O(d) arithmetic and O(d) output. The delivered row_contribution wrapper first validates the whole k×d dictionary and the k-entry amount row through nonnegative_table and real_table: that copies/scans O(kd+k) input cells. Its end-to-end time is therefore O(kd+k), with O(kd+k+d) temporary/output storage, rather than O(d). This safety cost avoids trusting caller state; an internal validated kernel can reuse validated factors without those copies. Requested all-row reconstruction takes O(nkd) arithmetic, and its n×d output is itself a storage cost."
        ]
      ]
